Ze-Reviewed-Against: github.com/vishvananda/netlink v1.3.1

parseXfrmState refuses a message shorter than struct xfrm_usersa_info
before it reads the header. Upstream hands the buffer to
nl.DeserializeXfrmUsersaInfo, which slices it to SizeofXfrmUsersaInfo with
no length check, so a truncated reply either panics or is decoded from
bytes past its end.

Its test, TestXfrmStateParseTruncatedHeader in
xfrm_state_truncated_linux_test.go, calls the parser for every short length,
the empty reply included, and checks that a complete header is accepted.

No upstream pull request is opened yet for this change.

Needs no earlier patch.

Applies unchanged to upstream main (e0e26cd, 2026-11-13), on its own, and its
test passes there unprivileged.

Delete this patch when go.mod requires an upstream release that contains the
change.

diff --git a/vendor/github.com/vishvananda/netlink/xfrm_state_linux.go b/vendor/github.com/vishvananda/netlink/xfrm_state_linux.go
--- a/vendor/github.com/vishvananda/netlink/xfrm_state_linux.go
+++ b/vendor/github.com/vishvananda/netlink/xfrm_state_linux.go
@@ -539,6 +539,9 @@
